metropolitan police commissioner  cressida dick has apologized to the  family of nicole smallman and bieber  henry for failings into the way police  handled missing persons reports about  the sisters after advice following an  independent office for police conduct  investigations the sisters had been  celebrating a birthday last june when  they were attacked and stabbed to death  in wembley in north west london uh  cressida dick said in a statement my  thoughts and deepest sympathies are with  the family and friends of nicole and  bieber for their tragic losses the way  we responded to information that nicole  and bieber were missing that weekend was  below the standard we should have  achieved and compounded the distress  felt by their loved ones  while we know that very sadly nicole and  bieber had been murdered in the early  hours of saturday june the 6th 2020  before they were reported missing if we  had responded better we may have saved  their friends and family immeasurable  pain  she continues i'm very sorry that the  level of service we provided fell short  we have contacted the family to ask if  they will allow me or if they prefer  another senior officer to visit them at  a time that is right to apologize in  person  that's uh from the commissioner of the  metropolitan police
 

